 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Relates to the creation of an early learning investment commission; provides support for public and private investment in early learning for children up to the age of five.",
 "title": "Relates to the creation of an early learning investment commission",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A6629",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A6629-2015",
     "printNo": "A6629",
     "session": 2015,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 208\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 6629, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  social  services  law,  in relation to the\n      creation of the early learning investment commission\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would establish a new early learning  investment  commission\nto make recommendations to improve early learning programs and to engage\nbusiness  and civic organizations in early learning planning and advoca-\ncy.\n\n  I vetoed substantially similar legislation last year  (Veto  Memo  No.\n544  of  2014).  While  I agree that early learning and education initi-\natives are critically important, this bill  is  unnecessary  because  it\nduplicates  efforts made by the State's Early Childhood Advisory Council\n(ECAC). The ECAC is already charged with  soliciting  input  and  making\nstrategic   recommendations  regarding  improvement  of  early  learning\nservices in New York State. As a result, I  again  cannot  approve  this\nbill.\n\n  Nonetheless,  I am directing the State agencies serving on the ECAC to\ncontinue working with private businesses and philanthropic  entities  to\ndevelop recommendations on public and private investment in early learn-\ning  so that in New York State, every child has the support and services\nnecessary to succeed in school and in life.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 208,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2015
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
